"use strict";(self.webpackChunkspa_template=self.webpackChunkspa_template||[]).push([[814],{2814:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"created":"2016-04-09T11:14:00","modified":"2016-04-09T11:14:00","id":1027,"title":"Released PDFManager version 1.4.1","article":"<p>I use a lot of pdfs to store pictures and documents, so I started developing myself a PDFManager to allow manipulation of existing PDF&#39;s and images. It is available as <a href=\\"https://github.com/lski/PdfManager\\">source code</a> and to <a href=\\"http://github.com/lski/PdfManager/releases/download/v1.4.1/PdfManagerSetup-1.4.1.exe\\">download</a> free as an exe.</p>\\n<p><img src=\\"https://lski-web-api.azurewebsites.net/uploaded/pdfmanager/PDFManager.png\\" alt=\\"PDF Manager UI\\"></p>\\n<p>You have several options, you can combine different images and PDF&#39;s together in the order specified, split a PDF, rotate the pages of a PDF or PDF&#39;s or convert images. It supports drag and drop of multiple files into the source file sections, also in batch sections like above it allows for re-ordering and deleting of source files.</p>\\n<p>Underneath the UI is a service layer that wraps around the PDFSharp package that is available via nuget and is open source and enables the manipulation of PDF files.</p>\\n<h2 id=\\"references\\">References</h2>\\n<ul>\\n<li><a href=\\"https://github.com/lski/PdfManager\\">source code on github</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\"http://github.com/lski/PdfManager/releases/download/v1.4.1/PdfManagerSetup-1.4.1.exe\\">download</a></li>\\n<li><a href=\\"http://www.pdfsharp.net/\\">PDFSharp home page</a></li>\\n</ul>\\n","showInResults":true,"tags":["pdf"]}')}}]);